Added the ``service.view_orphan_content`` permission, granted domain-scoped via the ``service.domain_admin`` and ``service.domain_viewer`` roles. Under RBAC (``PulpServiceAccessPolicy``), content reads are scoped by repository membership, which hides orphan (not-yet-in-a-repository) content and breaks read-after-upload flows. A user holding this permission for a domain can now view repository-less content in that domain, e.g. a package they just uploaded but have not yet added to a repository (requires pulpcore patch 0064).
